{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1539334-essence-pyros-and-sekhem","id":1539334,"title":"Essence, Pyros, and Sekhem.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-07-26T11:51:30-07:00","id":1539334,"title":"Essence, Pyros, and Sekhem.","content":"I want to know what is the difference between these three thing are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-26T13:23:53-07:00","id":1539336,"title":"","content":"Essence is the energy that the material world produces, relevant to memory and emotion and magical sustenance, that keeps ghosts, spirits, goetia, God-Machine angels, and other invisible entities active (as well as fueling the spiritual powers of the werewolves from Werewolf: the Forsaken and the Purified immortals from World of Darkness: Immortals and later Mummy: the Curse 2nd Edition); it is loosely identified with the Ka in the ancient Egyptian soul anatomy used in Mummy and less prominently in other gamelines (the Vampire clanbook Shadows in the Dark: Mekhet has an in-character primer on the subject refer to the Ka as the Soul of Sustenance). It is, as consistently described, equal parts food, currency, and oxygen to the ephemeral beings that truck with it.<br /> <br /> Sekhem is the stuff of manifest existence that differentiates into the Pillars Mummy uses as its more expendable fuel source; the Pillars are themselves what give rise to the things controlled by the Subtle Arcana (and their corresponding Gross Arcana) in Mage: the Awakening, e.g. the Pillar of the Name gives rise to Fate and Time and the things that those Arcana describe and affect, the Pillar of the Heart generates Spirit and Life, etc. The Mage/Mummy crossover material in Dark Eras likens the Shan-iatu's manipulation of raw Sekhem to handling plutonium with one's bare hands.<br /> <br /> Pyros is essentially an energy/substance that produces/embodies change. The two different &quot;flavors&quot; of Pyros, Elpis and Flux, resonate with changes in the constructive/creative/uplifting/inspiring and destructive/mutative/calcifying/horrifying directions, respectively, and Azoth, as a rarer type of Pyros, essentially works as an aggregative feedback loop that collects more Pyros and animates the Created. It is a volatile substance, as evidenced by its role in the creation of Prometheans and all their attendant side-effects as well as the various for-want-of-a-nail changes the qashmallim produce as manifestations of the Divine Fire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-26T19:26:58-07:00","id":1539359,"title":"","content":"I thought Pyros is the stuff of creation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-26T19:50:18-07:00","id":1539360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1539334-essence-pyros-and-sekhem?p=1539359#post1539359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought Pyros is the stuff of creation?</div> </div> </div> </div>Pyros is the fluid substance of purposeful change. It can bring the animate to life, but it's not going to create material <i>ex nihilo</i> \u2014 it's a brush, not a canvas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-26T19:57:01-07:00","id":1539361,"title":"","content":"Is Pyros connected to Glamour or the Wyrd?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-26T20:16:32-07:00","id":1539362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1539334-essence-pyros-and-sekhem?p=1539361#post1539361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is Pyros connected to Glamour or the Wyrd?</div> </div> </div> </div>Only in the sense that most supernatural power sources in the Chronicles convey, conduct, or express emotion in some fashion. The Wyrd is a force of reciprocity and Glamour is feelings made manifest. Pyros might make a person paranoid, but the Pyros isn't the feeling of paranoia any more than the glass of beer you have at dinner is the hangover you experience the next morning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-28T09:54:04-07:00","id":1539424,"title":"","content":"I think you have a stalker, Satchel. But I like your explanations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"